        "notes": "Open on present-day Hyde Park and Kenwood residential streets, slow tracking past brick three-flats and graystones that would have carried covenant clauses. Capture a 360 node at a Woodlawn corner near 6140 South Rhodes Avenue (Washington Park subdivision), exterior only, to anchor the Hansberry case. Film the University of Chicago campus edge where it meets the surrounding neighborhoods to underscore the institutional role. B-roll suggestions: archival-style inserts of a deed page and Great Migration rail imagery if licensed, otherwise hold on present-day storefronts and the 53rd Street corridor. No talking-head beat for this history chapter; narration carries it. End on a quiet exterior of a Kenwood block to hand off to the urban renewal chapter.",
